90\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/business/2026/03/14/ethereum-foundation-sells-5-000-ether-to-tom-lee-s-bitmine-in-usd10-2-million-deal\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"ETH sales\\\"]}],\\\" and narrow its focus to CROPS: censorship resistance, capture resistance, openness, privacy and security.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"88612b61bf9d\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"In a lengthy \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"c936707c5b39\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://x.com/i/status/2058583593102844111\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"post on X\\\"]}],\\\", Buterin detailed that the Ethereum Foundation holds roughly 0.16% of all ETH, well below the 10% to 50% he said it’s common for the central foundations of other blockchains to hold.\\\"]}],\\\"$L9b\\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"546ff032cecd\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Nearly 90% of his own net worth sits in ETH, with the remaining roughly $40 million in onchain fiat already earmarked for open-source biotech, software and hardware initiatives, Buterin added.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"a1370d908481\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"His influence within the EF will continue to decrease as the board expands, aligning with his desire to be less influential there. However, he also hedged his words, saying, \\\\\\\"This is only my own view. The board is not just me, and I have no extra special powers on the board that the other board members do not.\\\\\\\"\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"c3494eb86311\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"He framed the EF as \\\\\\\"one node, with a defined purpose, alongside other nodes,\\\\\\\" not the center of Ethereum. Addressing throughput, Buterin said it would be a mistake for Ethereum to maximize it.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L9c\\\",\\\"b950fa21\\\",{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"media\\\":\\\"desktop\\\",\\\"isPremium\\\":false}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0dabc2703069\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"“Being as fast and as scalable as possible, and only a small epsilon more decentralized than the others, is a route to mediocrity, and if we try it, we will lose.”\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"a056c732c46c\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Instead, Buterin pointed to Ethereum striving to be “deeply impressive” in what he called the “CROPS dimension.” That involves making Ethereum provably bug-free, which is argued to be within reach given AI-powered verification.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"d0f6827a668f\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"The post landed after at least 8 senior EF contributors left or announced departures in 2026, 5 in May alone, \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"d69406e4ed7c\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/tech/2026/05/20/the-protocol-ethereum-foundation-s-high-profile-departures-spark-fresh-debate\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"reigniting debate\\\"]}],\\\" over the foundation's direction.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"96e6c296d428\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-headline-sm font-medium\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Crypto community reacts\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"ccbe3f4f8e9d\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Prominent Ethereum voices were supportive of Buterin. \\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1cc65c8abe36\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"Anthony Sassano, an independent Ethereum educator, angel investor and advisor, \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"06cbc212ace3\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://x.com/sassal0x/status/2058658863650668962\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"replied directly\\\"]}],\\\" to the post, thanking Buterin. A \\\",\\\"$L9d\\\",\\\" from Sassano focused on Buterin's framing of ETH as the most high-value \\\\\\\"product\\\\\\\" of the Ethereum blockchain.\\\"]}],\\\"$L9e\\\",\\\"$L9f\\\",\\\"$La0\\\",\\\"$La1\\\",\\\"$La2\\\",\\\"$La3\\\",\\\"$La4\\\",\\\"$La5\\\",\\\"$La6\\\"]}]}],null]}],\\\"$La7\\\",\\\"$La8\\\"]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"aa:I[72156,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3aa2a9bcdbf11175.js?dpl=dpl_52NxQdYNBFABzdhRhkLx88s2N5N2\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0